{"name":"Rosa Vieja","hex":"#f0e3df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to hide, vanish, shadow"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["no-show, someone who does not show up as expected"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vieja","blocks":[{"text":"Vieja is a genus of cichlid fish from Central America and Mexico. The majority of the species are freshwater fish found in stagnant or slow-moving waters of southern Mexico to El Salvador, but V. maculicauda, which also occurs in brackish waters, ranges south to Panama. They are high-bodied cichlids that reach lengths of up to 17–35 cm (7–14 in) depending on the exact species. Vieja feed mostly on vegetable matter, but may also take small invertebrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Vieja_maculicauda.jpg/330px-Vieja_maculicauda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vieja"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg/500px-Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg/1280px-Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg/500px-Vieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVieja_melanura_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg"}],"sounds":{"rosa":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/En-us-rosa.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_conten